SUMMARY:Bent Creek--Rice Pinnacle--Stradley Mountain Loop  9.7 miles\, 130
 0 ft ascent
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**Trailhead: Rice Pinnacle\, Bent 
 Creek**\n**Description**: Good footing\, mostly shaded\, gradual ascent. T
 ake the Deer Lake Lodge trail to Wolf Branch Trail to Ledford Trail (R) to
  Road 479 (R) to left on Rice Pinnacle Rd (491) and start of climb. At Ing
 les Field Gap take a sharp left on trail of the same name and ascend to Fo
 ur corners--Stradley Mt. Take Little Hickory Top and descend to Ledford Ga
 p and snack at picnic tables. Take Boyd Branch to Campground Connector\, B
 ent Creek Gap Rd to Wesley Branch Trailhead. Deer Lake Lodge Trail back to
  Rice Pinnacle. Type: Loop. Max Elev: 3000'. Avg moving pace: 2.3 mph. Dog
 s on leash OK\n**Lunch is an option following the hike! Come join me for m
 y last hike of the season before heading back to FL**\n\\*\\*COURTESY (Ple
 ase read carefully!)\\*\\* Only sign up if you \\\\\\*truly\\\\\\* plan to
  come. If you must cancel\, please change your status to "Not Going" as so
 on as possible. Avoid dropping out last-minute so that wait-listers can ha
 ve sufficient notice. And please please PLEASE don't be a no-show\n\n**LEG
 ALESE**\nThis Asheville Hiking Group event involves hiking and\, possibly\
 , transportation to and from the meetup site. Participants are responsible
  for their own safety and affirm that they have the appropriate skills\, p
 hysical conditioning\, equipment\, and supplies. Hiking may involve risks 
 to oneself and property. Neither your hike organizer nor Asheville Hiking 
 Group can assure your safety nor eliminate all risks. Participants assume 
 full responsibility for any injuries\, damages\, or losses.
