SUMMARY:Bull Creek & Swannanoa River\, 6.6 mi\, 400 ft elevation gain
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**[Sign-up opens 8:00 PM\, Sunday 
 October 18th]**\n\nOur route for this hike loops around the Bull Creek Pre
 serve before branching off onto the Dam Pasture Connector trail. This take
 s us to the Swannanoa River trail\, then over to the lovely Warren Wilson 
 campus. There\, at around our halfway point\, we'll take a snack and water
  break and return the same way.\n\nThe total distance is around 6.6 miles 
 with a 425' elevation gain. We'll amble at a 2.5 mph clip. This is a relat
 ively tame hike with a rating of about 3 on a 1-10 scale. Big shout-out to
  Todd for piecing this trail together and sharing it with me.\n\n***Dog Po
 licy:*** Dogs are extremely welcome but must be leashed.\n\n***Guest Polic
 y:*** If you'd like to bring a guest\, they should join the Asheville Hiki
 ng Group and sign up for the hike on their own. Alternatively\, contact me
  in advance and ask if it's okay to bring a "+1" after you've made it onto
  the "Going" list. Depending on timing and demand\, I MAY be able to add y
 our guest.\n\n**MEET-UP TIME AND PLACE**\nThe trailhead is across the stre
 et from Berea Baptist Church\, 2578 Riceville Rd\, Asheville. There is som
 e parking at the trailhead\, and additional space in the church parking lo
 t.\n\n**[Click here for a map to our meetup location.](https://maps.app.go
 o.gl/1s25Xjnx63CRKdJM8)**[ ](https://maps.app.goo.gl/1s25Xjnx63CRKdJM8)\n\
 n**COURTESY TO WAIT-LISTERS (Please abide!)**\nOnly sign up if you \\*TRUL
 Y\\* plan to come. If you must cancel\, please change your status to "Not 
 Going" as soon as possible so wait-listers will have sufficient notice. An
 d please please PLEASE don't be a no-show.\n\nIf you're on the waiting lis
 t\, keep checking the evening before. Despite my impassioned pleas\, we us
 ually have last-minute dropouts.\n\n**WEATHER**\nI'll monitor National Wea
 ther Service forecasts for the hike area and email cancellation messages b
 y 7:30 AM if the forecast is for more than a 50% chance of precipitation.\
 n\n**QUESTIONS?**\nIf you have any questions\, message me through MeetUp u
 ntil 8:30 AM the day of.\n\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\
 \-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n**LEGALESE**\nThis Asheville Hiking Group event involves h
 iking and\, possibly\, transportation to and from the meetup site. Partici
 pants are responsible for their own safety and\, by joining a hike\, affir
 m that they have the appropriate skills\, physical conditioning\, equipmen
 t\, and supplies. Hiking may involve risks to oneself and property. Neithe
 r your hike organizer nor Asheville Hiking Group can eliminate all risks o
 r be responsible for your well-being. Participants assume full responsibil
 ity for any injuries\, damages\, or losses.
